# CHANGELOG discipline for this project

Whenever you modify ANY of the following in this repository, you MUST append a
new entry at the top of `CHANGELOG.md` before ending your turn:

- Backend code (`website/app.py`, `website/content_model.py`,
  `phishing-detection/src/**`)
- Frontend code (`website/static/**`)
- Datasets (`phishing-detection/data/**`)
- Notebooks (`phishing-detection/notebooks/**`)
- Project documentation (`README.md`, `phishing-detection/README.md`)
- Dependencies (`*requirements.txt`)
- Cursor rules, `.cursor/**`, or this file itself

## Entry format (newest first, Pacific time)

```
## [YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM PT] — Short title

### Why
- 1–3 bullets explaining the motivation / observed problem / user request.

### Files changed
- `path/to/file.py` — concrete one-line description per file
- ...

### Effect
- Concrete before/after metrics, behavioural changes, or sample-level
  evidence. Use tables when comparing model versions.
```

## Rules

1. **Always at the top.** The most recent entry is the first entry under the
   "Format is loosely based on..." line.
2. **Be specific.** Reference exact file paths, function names, metric values,
   sample inputs, dataset row counts. Avoid generic phrases like "improved
   accuracy"; quote the number.
3. **Group atomically.** A single logical change (even spanning many files)
   is ONE entry. Multiple unrelated changes in the same turn get multiple
   entries.
4. **Never delete history.** If a previous entry is wrong, add a follow-up
   entry that corrects it rather than editing the old one.
5. **No emojis in headings**, but ✓ / ⚠ inline inside tables is fine.
6. If a change is purely cosmetic (typo, indent, comment-only) you may skip the
   entry, but anything that would affect a reviewer must be logged.
